# =============================================================================
# Imposter Game — root environment template
# =============================================================================
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to .env in the repository root:
#        cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in real values. NEVER commit .env (it is gitignored).
#   3. Only variables listed here should exist in the project. This file is the
#      single source of truth for environment variable NAMES.
#
# WHERE ENV FILES LIVE
#   .env.example (this file)   committed  → template + documentation for humans
#   .env                       gitignored → your real local values
#   apps/server/.env           gitignored → server-only values (optional, overrides)
#   apps/web/.env.local        gitignored → Next.js local values (optional)
#   apps/mobile/.env           gitignored → Expo local values (optional)
#
# RULES
#   - Empty assignments are fine; empty secrets are not.
#   - Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ or EXPO_PUBLIC_ IS SHIPPED TO THE BROWSER /
#     APP BUNDLE and is therefore PUBLIC. Never put a secret behind those prefixes.
#   - Server secrets must have NO public prefix.
#   - Keep this file alphabetically grouped and documented as it grows.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=development

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKEND — apps/server
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the Socket.IO + HTTP server listens on.
PORT=4000

# Full origin allowed to open cross-origin socket connections.
# Comma-separate multiple origins in development if both web and a device
# on your LAN need access, e.g.:
#   CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://192.168.1.20:8081
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEB APP — apps/web (Next.js)
# PUBLIC: exposed to the browser bundle. Fine for a socket URL, never a secret.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOBILE APP — apps/mobile (Expo)
# PUBLIC: exposed to the app bundle.
# NOTE: "localhost" from a physical device means THE DEVICE ITSELF. On a real
# phone you must use your machine's LAN IP (e.g. http://192.168.1.20:4000),
# or a tunnel. An Android emulator reaches the host via http://10.0.2.2:4000.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FUTURE / NOT USED YET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The project has no database, no auth and no cache today. When (if) those
# arrive, add their variables here with a clear comment, for example:
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/imposter_game
#   REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
#
# Do not add them before the code that reads them exists.
